in @prism
in @meta
in @epistemologic

# @epistemologic/cybernetic — the substrate's discipline for declarative
# cybernetic properties.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-09, Reed + Alex; cybernetic foundation landed
# at systemic.engineering `f9e0402`, 1,659 lines): cybernetics-the-
# tradition belongs at the substrate altitude as a family of *declarative
# properties* that shards can name, distinct from cybernetics-the-CS-
# shadow (the feedback-loop synonym). The eleven canonical primitives —
# Ashby's requisite variety, Conant-Ashby's good regulator, Beer's
# viable-system five-function audit, the Beer / Reyes algedonic channel,
# Bateson's three learning levels, Maturana-Varela's autopoiesis, von
# Foerster's second-order observer, Spencer-Brown's distinction, Pask's
# conversation, Glanville's design-IS-cybernetics, von Foerster /
# Kauffman's eigenform — all live here, sited as `@epistemologic/
# cybernetic/X`.
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# A cybernetic property declares a substrate-altitude obligation a shard
# names ABOUT ITSELF or about a contract it holds with another shard. The
# obligation is *verifiable at the species boundary* (the
# `@code/metalogue/materialize.classify` discriminator surface) when
# mechanical; *transitively verifiable* when the discipline reduces to
# lower-altitude checks; *cross-tick verifiable* when the cascade audit
# is the discharge.
#
# The family is the cybernetic complement to the `@mirror/cybernetics/X`
# operational family. Alex's bilateral framing: declarative property here,
# operational primitive at `@mirror/cybernetics/X`. The seam maps to four
# cybernetic distinctions simultaneously (von Foerster first/second-order;
# Maturana structure/organisation; Beer S3/S4; Pask M-individual/P-
# individual) — the convergence of four traditions at one architectural
# seam is what makes the substrate's instantiation novel.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Currently landed:
#
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/variety       Ashby 1956 §11/7. The shard's
#                                           declared variety vector with
#                                           per-axis budget. The first
#                                           cybernetic property; the
#                                           shape teaches the structure
#                                           for the next ten.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform     von Foerster 1981; Kauffman
#                                           2003. The identity carrier
#                                           IS the fixed point of a
#                                           recursive structure
#                                           (seed, iteration, witness).
#                                           Inherited by the
#                                           forward-promised species
#                                           `@cyberpunk/distinction`,
#                                           `@cyberpunk/second_order`,
#                                           `@cyberpunk/autopoiesis`
#                                           per recursion-lock-tower
#                                           audit §8.8.1 / §12.5.
#                                           Recognition #38;
#                                           `uuid_spectral` is the
#                                           load-bearing prior
#                                           instance.
#
# Pending — land when a consumer pulls (substrate-pull-urgency order per
# the cybernetic foundation §5.3):
#
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/good_regulator   Conant-Ashby 1970. The
#                                              shard structure is a
#                                              homomorphic image of the
#                                              system it regulates. The
#                                              round-trip law on the
#                                              metalogue shims IS this
#                                              property's verifiable
#                                              shape.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/viable           Beer 1972, 1979, 1985. The
#                                              shard carries all five
#                                              VSM functions at its
#                                              altitude.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/algedonic        Beer 1972; Reyes et al.
#                                              2024. Bilateral with
#                                              @mirror/cybernetics/
#                                              algedonic. Failure
#                                              verdicts carry structured
#                                              bypass payload.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction      Spencer-Brown 1969. The
#                                              substrate's deepest stack
#                                              layer; grounds `gap`,
#                                              `transparency`, `\`.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation     Pask 1975, 1976. `requires`
#                                              clauses ARE bilateral
#                                              agreements between P-
#                                              individuals.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning Bateson 1972. Three sub-
#                                              properties: learning_I /
#                                              learning_II / learning_III.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis      Maturana-Varela 1980. The
#                                              substrate's bidirectional
#                                              production fixed point.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order     von Foerster 1981. The
#                                              shard's model includes
#                                              itself.
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/design           Glanville 1982, 2007. The
#                                              shard's design history
#                                              is part of its content.
#                                              Per the foundation §4.3:
#                                              NO `@mirror/cybernetics/
#                                              design` operational
#                                              sibling; design IS
#                                              constitutively second-
#                                              order and lives in the
#                                              cascade itself.
#
# === Why a family root ===
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] every kind that stands
# on its own discipline is a prism. `cybernetic` IS such a kind: a
# substrate-wide vocabulary for declarative cybernetic obligations, with
# a shared verification discipline (species-boundary check at
# `@code/metalogue/materialize.classify`), a shared bilateral framing
# (property here / operation at `@mirror/cybernetics/X`), and eleven
# species that each carry their own contract under the same discipline.
#
# The previous shape (cybernetic primitives implicit in the substrate-pull
# cascade, named only in prose) under-declared the inheritance. The
# family root makes the discipline explicit; species inherit through
# `in @epistemologic/cybernetic` at the top of their files (cf. the
# @epistemologic/reality precedent, 2026-06-06).
#
# === Substrate-pull recognitions grounded here ===
#
# Recognition #36 (Reed, mirror `1ad45b4`): Ashby's law in multi-
# dimensional variety space. Grounds `variety`.
# Recognition #37 (Reed, promoted 2026-06-09): every `requires` clause is
# a Pask agreement. Grounds the future `conversation` property.
# Recognition #38 (Reed, promoted 2026-06-09): `uuid_spectral` IS an
# eigenform. Grounds the future `eigenform` property.
# Recognition #39 (Reed, promoted 2026-06-09): the substrate-pull
# discipline IS Glanville's cybernetic design. Grounds the future
# `design` property.
# Recognition #40 (Reed, promoted 2026-06-09): the bilateral property/
# operation seam IS Maturana's structure/organisation. Grounds the
# discipline of the family itself.
# Recognition #41 (Reed, promoted 2026-06-09): the cybernetic-property
# family lift IS a Learning III event at the substrate altitude. Grounds
# the family ROOT (this file).
#
# Spec context: systemic.engineering `f9e0402`
#               (practice/insights/cybernetics/
#                2026-06-09-cybernetic-foundation-for-mirror-substrate.md),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-09-ashby-multi-dimensional-variety-
#               sub-turing-epistemologic.md (recognition #36).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (prior
#                       Ashby citation in the @io context — the
#                       multi-axis lift extends this).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror (the first
#                 species; landed alongside this root),
#                 boot/02-epistemologic.mirror (the @epistemologic
#                 grammar this family inherits from),
#                 epistemologic/reality.mirror (the precedent family-root
#                 shape; same pattern).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/cybernetic` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic {
  focus cybernetic
  project cybernetic
  split cybernetic
  shift cybernetic
  settle cybernetic
}

out @epistemologic/cybernetic
